Part A: Pirillo Pipes Attribution & Commercial Revenue Grant

This is the operative custom license for Pirillo Pipes. The rights holders
making Pirillo Pipes available through Pirillo Studio (the Licensor) grant
these permissions only for rights they own or are authorized to license.
Part B below is an unmodified reference copy only, not an alternative license
for Pirillo Pipes and not a source of additional permissions for it.

1. Permission

Subject to the conditions below, you may use, reproduce, modify and distribute
Pirillo Pipes, including in hosted SaaS and web applications, development
pipelines, commercial products and media. Noncommercial use is royalty-free.
Commercial use is royalty-free through the revenue threshold in section 3.

2. Mandatory public attribution

Any public-facing product, website, application, pipeline output, content or
repository built with or powered by Pirillo Pipes must display this exact,
clear, visible credit:

Built on Pirillo Pipes by Pirillo Studio

Link the credit to https://github.com/ChrisPirillo/pirillo-pipes or
https://github.com/ChrisPirillo/pirillo-studio. Display it in the primary user
interface or footer, in the public description, and in accompanying
documentation. For a public work without a user interface, include the credit
with the published output or its description and documentation. Attribution
is required for both noncommercial and commercial uses, including uses below
the revenue threshold. A hidden source comment or private record is not a
substitute for this public credit.

When distributing Pirillo Pipes or modified copies, include this LICENSE and
NOTICE, and retain applicable copyright, license and third-party notices.

3. Commercial revenue share

For each commercial project built with or powered by Pirillo Pipes, the first
$10,000 USD of lifetime gross project revenue is royalty-free. Above that
threshold, contribute 5% of the gross revenue exceeding $10,000 USD to the
LockerGnome, or obtain a separate custom commercial license
from Pirillo Studio that covers that use.

Gross project revenue means all revenue generated by the covered product,
service, pipeline or commercial content before expenses or other deductions.
The threshold applies over the project's lifetime, not separately each year.
The total contribution due is 0.05 times the amount by which lifetime gross
project revenue exceeds $10,000 USD, less contributions already made under
this section. For example, $12,000 USD of lifetime gross project revenue
requires a total contribution of $100 USD. Noncommercial use remains
royalty-free.

Contact Pirillo Studio through the maintainers of the Pirillo Studio
repository above for contribution instructions or a custom commercial license.

4. Conditions and scope

These permissions are conditional on compliance with this Part A. Commercial
use that fails its attribution or revenue-share conditions is not authorized
by this grant, unless a separate valid license authorizes it. Part B does not
provide a fallback permission for Pirillo Pipes. Rights available under law
without a license are unaffected.

This grant does not revoke valid licenses already granted for earlier copies,
or replace licenses and notices applicable to separately licensed third-party
material. LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 preserves the previous repository license text;
it is not a new Apache grant for material licensed only under this Part A.
Source provenance is recorded in docs/provenance.json.

5. Names, brands and modified versions

Except for the required attribution and lawful factual references, this grant
does not grant permission to use the Licensor's or contributors' names,
trademarks or logos, including those of Pirillo Pipes, Pirillo Studio or
LockerGnome. You must not imply that
they created, sponsor or endorse your product, service, content or modified
version without separate permission. Identify modified versions as modified
and do not present them as official Pirillo Pipes releases. The required
"Built on" credit identifies the underlying software; it is not an endorsement.

6. No warranty or liability

As far as the law permits, Pirillo Pipes is provided as is, without warranties
or conditions of any kind. The Licensor is not liable for damages arising
from its use or these terms.

